            <div class="row justify-between gap-12">
                <!-- Text -->
                <div class="col flex-basis-60" data-basis-100="768">
                    <p>
                        Most breweries have a story behind every beer. Sometimes the story has a mission and can help
                        build your breweries mission, or sometimes it’s a goof and can simply create a point of
                        discussion amongst your local community. No matter the purpose, my process begins by
                        understanding how the idea came to light and asking:
                    </p>
                    <p class="callout">
                        “How can we make this more than just a beer label? How do we turn this into a merch
                        opportunity?”
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Over the years I’ve explored, designed, and launched beers with all types of artwork styles.
                        From characters and mascots to landscapes. Pattern heavy designs to simple iconography. Detailed
                        line-work to letter heavy designs. Regardless of the style, the artwork is always in vector
                        format, and designed in a way to easily translate to other colaterral.
                        <br><br>
                        Small brewpubs who prefer to sell their packaged product at the source instead of distributing
                        have a unique opportunity to be experimental with their labeling. When you distribute your
                        product, consistency helps consumers easily identify your brand on the crowded shelf. But if
                        your consumers are already in your establishment, you're not competing for shelf space, giving
                        you the space and opportunity to get creative in your products.

                    </p>

                </div>
